We have seen a few sub-10000 turn YAAP's on this board, but we don't
see too many tries at "fastest" ascensions anymore.  Also, you don't
see anyone trying for a sub-10K tourist, samurai, or caveman.

Here's what I propose to do about it:

Make February "Exploring Fast Ascensions" month.
The members of r.g.r.n will be encouraged to start games in "explore"
mode (starting with a wand of wishing) to simulate extreme early luck.
However, they will be limited to using 7 wishes (just to keep it fair).
Some people would use all 7 wishes from the starting wand, requiring
perhaps 100 turns to wrest the last wish, while others would probably
use 6 from the begining and then use the castle wand or a magic lamp
for the last one.

This way, I would expect to see sub-10K ascensions in every class.  It
would be interesting to see how close some players can get to the ~2100
turn theoretical limit.

I know that most of the hardcore players here frown on explore mode for
anything other than brief tests, but I think this could be fun and
educational.

What say you all?


